0
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,604
Tyra: PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"...

1
00:00:03,604 --> 00:00:05,572
SHANDI STRUGGLED TO LEAVE
HER PAST AS A CLERK

2
00:00:05,572 --> 00:00:07,074
AT WALGREENS BEHIND...

3
00:00:07,074 --> 00:00:08,876
Shandi: I'M GOING TO DO
ANYTHING TO CHANGE MY LIFE.

4
00:00:08,876 --> 00:00:09,943
Camille: WHAT ARE YOU
HEARING?

5
00:00:09,943 --> 00:00:11,745
Yoanna: I DON'T TRUST YOU.

6
00:00:11,745 --> 00:00:13,881
Tyra: WHILE CAMILLE SPARKED
TENSIONS WITH HER COMPETITORS,

7
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:16,817
AND SARA DISOBEYED
HER FATHER'S WISHES.

8
00:00:16,817 --> 00:00:18,952
Sara: HE CONSIDERS
MODELING PROSTITUTION.

9
00:00:18,952 --> 00:00:20,821
Tyra: MERCEDES KEPT
HER ILLNESS A SECRET

10
00:00:20,821 --> 00:00:22,222
FROM EVERYONE.

11
00:00:22,222 --> 00:00:25,592
AND IN THE LAST ELIMINATION,
JENASCIA WAS SENT HOME.

12
00:00:25,592 --> 00:00:26,793
EIGHT GIRLS REMAIN.

13
00:00:26,793 --> 00:00:29,997
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

14
00:00:29,997 --> 00:00:33,634
♪♪♪

15
00:01:06,266 --> 00:01:09,369
Catie: THE PAST ELIMINATIONS
I'M FEELING RELIEVED.

16
00:01:09,369 --> 00:01:11,772
I'M FEELING DISAPPOINTED
THAT I LET MYSELF SLIP

17
00:01:11,772 --> 00:01:13,540
DOWN THE RANKINGS.

18
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:15,943
I JUST REALIZED THAT I REALLY
NEED TO UP MY GAME.

19
00:01:15,943 --> 00:01:17,578
Camille: I MEAN, THEY CAN
CHOOSE, LIKE, A MILLION

20
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:19,913
BLONDE-HAIRED, BLUE-EYED GIRLS
TO WALK DOWN A RUNWAY,

21
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:23,817
BUT BLACK WOMEN IN A SHOW
ARE FAR AND FEW BETWEEN, OKAY?

22
00:01:23,817 --> 00:01:25,252
IT'S VERY COMPETITIVE.

23
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:26,420
IT'S, LIKE, THAT ONE TOKEN GIRL.

24
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:27,487
April: WELL, COME ON.

25
00:01:27,487 --> 00:01:28,488
WHAT PERCENTAGE
OF MAGAZINE COVERS

26
00:01:28,488 --> 00:01:29,756
DO YOU SEE AN ASIAN ON?

27
00:01:29,756 --> 00:01:31,358
IT'S ROUGHER BEING AN ASIAN
THAN A BLACK WOMAN.

28
00:01:31,358 --> 00:01:32,759
TYRA'S TOLD ME RIGHT UP FRONT.

29
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,361
Tyra: THE FASHION INDUSTRY
IS ALL ABOUT RACE.

30
00:01:34,361 --> 00:01:35,762
April: REALLY?

31
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,464
Tyra: DO YOU SEE ASIAN GIRLS
ON THE COVERS OF MAGAZINES?

32
00:01:37,464 --> 00:01:38,298
AND I'M NOT TALKING
ABOUT LUCY LIU.

33
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:39,499
SHE'S AN ACTRESS.

34
00:01:39,499 --> 00:01:40,968
SO YOU ENTERING
THIS FASHION WORLD--

35
00:01:40,968 --> 00:01:43,236
YOU WOULD BE AN UNDERDOG.

36
00:01:43,236 --> 00:01:45,205
April: BEFORE I DECIDED
TO ENTER INTO THIS INDUSTRY,

37
00:01:45,205 --> 00:01:46,974
I NEVER REALLY THOUGHT
ABOUT MY ETHNICITY.

38
00:01:46,974 --> 00:01:49,776
SHE SAID, "THERE'S LESS SLOTS
FOR YOU IN ANY RUNWAY SHOW,

39
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:52,512
EDITORIAL OF FASHION MAGAZINES
THAN ANY SINGLE OTHER RACE

40
00:01:52,512 --> 00:01:53,814
YOU CAN EVEN THINK OF
RIGHT NOW."

41
00:01:53,814 --> 00:01:56,350
I'M HALF JAPANESE,
AND I'M HALF CAUCASIAN,

42
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:58,819
BUT I'VE NEVER DONE ANYTHING
THAT MADE ME ASSOCIATE MYSELF

43
00:01:58,819 --> 00:02:01,355
AS AN ASIAN.

44
00:02:01,355 --> 00:02:02,889
Camille: I DON'T KNOW
HOW MUCH APRIL LIVES OUT

45
00:02:02,889 --> 00:02:04,658
HER JAPANESE CULTURE
IN HER LIFE,

46
00:02:04,658 --> 00:02:07,561
BUT HER JAPANESE HERITAGE
MIGHT BE THAT ONE THING

47
00:02:07,561 --> 00:02:09,963
THAT'S GONNA GIVE HER THE EDGE.

48
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:13,567
Mercedes: THAT'S NICE--
LET ME SEE.

49
00:02:13,567 --> 00:02:14,835
WHAT IS THAT?

50
00:02:14,835 --> 00:02:16,203
Sara: IT'S FROM IRAN.

51
00:02:16,203 --> 00:02:17,904
MOSQUES. IT'S HAND-PAINTED.

52
00:02:17,904 --> 00:02:20,674
I AM SO PROUD
OF MY PERSIAN CULTURE,

53
00:02:20,674 --> 00:02:24,544
BUT TO MY IRANIAN FAMILY--
MY FATHER, WHO'S MUSLIM,

54
00:02:24,544 --> 00:02:27,648
A MODEL IS A WHORE.

55
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:30,384
Mercedes: I GOTTA
DO SOMETHING.

56
00:02:30,384 --> 00:02:32,886
I WAS DIAGNOSED WITH LUPUS,
WHICH IS A CHRONIC ILLNESS THAT

57
00:02:32,886 --> 00:02:35,722
ATTACKS YOUR IMMUNE SYSTEM,
ABOUT A YEAR AGO,

58
00:02:35,722 --> 00:02:38,258
AND I DON'T WANT MY ROOMMATES
TO KNOW.

59
00:02:38,258 --> 00:02:39,760
I HIDE EVERYTHING.

60
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,895
I TAKE PILLS UNDER THE COUNTER,
AND, LIKE, HURRY UP

61
00:02:41,895 --> 00:02:43,230
AND DRINK SOME WATER.

62
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:44,698
I DON'T WANNA BE JUDGED.

63
00:02:44,698 --> 00:02:46,800
I JUST WANNA BE AS NORMAL
AS EVERYBODY ELSE.

64
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,870
♪♪♪

65
00:02:52,806 --> 00:02:54,741
Tyra: HELLO.

66
00:02:54,741 --> 00:02:55,676
LOOK AT YOU.

67
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:56,743
WHAT YOU DOIN'?

68
00:02:56,743 --> 00:02:58,345
OKAY, COME ON.

69
00:02:58,345 --> 00:03:01,014
WHOO! WHOO!

70
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,649
I CAN'T GET OUT.

71
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:03,517
AAH!

72
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:06,987
(laughter)

73
00:03:06,987 --> 00:03:08,588
Tyra: NOW I'M ALL HOT.

74
00:03:08,588 --> 00:03:10,257
OH, MY GOSH. COME OVER HERE.

75
00:03:10,257 --> 00:03:11,758
OKAY.

76
00:03:11,758 --> 00:03:12,893
YEAH, WE NEED TO GET
YOU GUYS SOME DOUBLE DUTCH.

77
00:03:12,893 --> 00:03:13,760
Mercedes: YEAH.

78
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,295
Tyra: OKAY.

79
00:03:15,295 --> 00:03:16,329
SO I'M REALLY PROUD OF YOU ALL.

80
00:03:16,329 --> 00:03:17,531
YOU GUYS ARE REALLY STRONG.

81
00:03:17,531 --> 00:03:19,566
FROM NOW ON,
IT'S GONNA BE REALLY DIFFICULT

82
00:03:19,566 --> 00:03:21,902
WITH THE ELIMINATIONS,
AND I CAN TELL AFTER JUDGING

83
00:03:21,902 --> 00:03:24,905
HOW HEAVY THE WHOLE EXPERIENCE
OF THIS COMPETITION

84
00:03:24,905 --> 00:03:27,541
IS REALLY WEIGHING ON YOU ALL.

85
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:30,711
SO I WANTED TO DO
A ONE-ON-ONE WITH EVERYBODY.

86
00:03:30,711 --> 00:03:32,279
SO LET'S START WITH XIOMARA.

87
00:03:32,279 --> 00:03:33,647
Xiomara: WHAT'S UP?

88
00:03:33,647 --> 00:03:34,614
YOU HAVE ANYTHING TO TELL ME
THAT I SHOULD--

89
00:03:34,614 --> 00:03:36,249
Tyra: I DO, ACTUALLY.
Xiomara: LET'S TALK.

90
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:38,819
Tyra: I LOVE YOUR TOUGHNESS,
AND I FEEL LIKE YOU'RE TRYING

91
00:03:38,819 --> 00:03:41,221
TO DO THIS FEMININE THING
THAT'S NOT NATURAL FOR YOU.

92
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,789
Xiomara: I WILL BE TOUGH.

93
00:03:42,789 --> 00:03:44,691
Tyra: I JUST FEEL LIKE THAT
IS WHAT MAKES YOU SPECIAL.

94
00:03:44,691 --> 00:03:46,293
Catie: I STILL NEED TO FIND
FIND COMFORT ZONE

95
00:03:46,293 --> 00:03:49,763
WITH STILL BEING ME,
BUT NOT LOOKING LIKE PLAIN JANE.

96
00:03:49,763 --> 00:03:51,698
Tyra: HOW ARE YOU HANDLING
YOUR STRESS AND PRESSURE?

97
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:53,266
Yoanna: BETTER. A LOT BETTER.

98
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:54,568
THE STRESS LEVEL IS NOT INTENSE.

99
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:56,336
I MEAN, I DO KINDA MISS MY MOM.

100
00:03:56,336 --> 00:03:57,504
Tyra: MY MOM AND I
ARE LIKE THIS.

101
00:03:57,504 --> 00:03:58,839
Yoanna: THAT'S LIKE MY MOM.

102
00:03:58,839 --> 00:04:01,508
Tyra: MY MOM QUIT HER JOB
AND CAME WITH ME TO PARIS

103
00:04:01,508 --> 00:04:04,377
WHEN I WAS 18,
AND SHE IS THE REASON WHY

104
00:04:04,377 --> 00:04:06,246
I'M STANDING IN FRONT OF YOU
RIGHT HERE TODAY.

105
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,849
MY MOM IS MY ROCK.

106
00:04:08,849 --> 00:04:10,250
Camille: OKAY.

107
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,585
THIS IS THE FIRST TIME
IN MY WHOLE ENTIRE LIFE

108
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:13,620
I HAVE EVER BEEN CALLED A DIVA.

109
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:15,989
Tyra: I SEE CAMILLE,
AND I SEE THE DIVA ATTITUDE.

110
00:04:15,989 --> 00:04:18,892
THERE'S A CERTAIN LEVEL
OF HUMILITY, MODESTY

111
00:04:18,892 --> 00:04:20,961
THAT YOU HAVE TO HAVE.

112
00:04:20,961 --> 00:04:23,764
IT'S NOT ABOUT PROVING TO
THE WORLD HOW GREAT YOU CAN BE

113
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:25,732
WITH THIS THING ON YOUR CHEST
LIKE, "I'M GOOD, I'M GOOD,

114
00:04:25,732 --> 00:04:26,933
I'M GOOD."

115
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,468
IT'S A QUIET CONFIDENCE.

116
00:04:28,468 --> 00:04:30,604
April: I BELIEVE MY CALLING
IN LIFE IS TO BE A SOURCE

117
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:32,639
OF INSPIRATION AND STRENGTH
TO OTHER PEOPLE, BECAUSE THAT'S

118
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:34,708
WHEN I FEEL SO GOOD.

119
00:04:34,708 --> 00:04:37,410
Tyra: I LOVE THAT YOU
SEE YOURSELF IN THAT WAY,

120
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:38,578
ESPECIALLY AS A WOMAN OF COLOR.

121
00:04:38,578 --> 00:04:39,646
YOU KNOW?

122
00:04:39,646 --> 00:04:40,981
April: I HAVEN'T
BEEN CONNECTED

123
00:04:40,981 --> 00:04:42,415
WITH MY JAPANESE HERITAGE,

124
00:04:42,415 --> 00:04:44,618
AND I'M NOT GONNA
PRETEND I HAVE.

125
00:04:44,618 --> 00:04:47,487
SO I'M NOT TRYING TO MARKET
MYSELF TO JUST ASIAN GIRLS.

126
00:04:47,487 --> 00:04:48,889
Sara: IT'S JUST,
I WANNA ASK YOUR OPINION ON WHAT

127
00:04:48,889 --> 00:04:50,757
I SHOULD DO ABOUT MY DAD,
BECAUSE HE'S LEAVING MESSAGES

128
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:52,425
ON MY CELL PHONE RIGHT NOW
AND CALLING MY MOM.

129
00:04:52,425 --> 00:04:53,560
Tyra: DOES HE KNOW
WHERE YOU ARE?

130
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,595
Sara: NO, HE DON'T.
Tyra: HE DOESN'T?

131
00:04:55,595 --> 00:04:57,597
WOULD IT HELP YOU IN ANY WAY,
WOULD IT GIVE YOU STRENGTH

132
00:04:57,597 --> 00:04:58,698
TO TALK TO HIM?

133
00:04:58,698 --> 00:04:59,800
Sara: TO TALK TO HIM
JUST LIKE...

134
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:02,636
Tyra: WHETHER IT'S
A CURSE-OUT OR A...

135
00:05:02,636 --> 00:05:05,372
Sara: IT WOULD BE OVER
IF I TALKED TO HIM RIGHT NOW.

136
00:05:05,372 --> 00:05:06,706
Tyra: IT MIGHT BE SOMETHING
THAT YOU HAVE TO DEAL WITH.

137
00:05:06,706 --> 00:05:08,742
MAYBE IN YOUR PHOTO SHOOTS
YOU ARE THINKING ABOUT HIM.

138
00:05:08,742 --> 00:05:10,343
THERE'S AN ANGER,
BUT THERE'S MAYBE A SADNESS,

139
00:05:10,343 --> 00:05:11,812
'CAUSE THAT'S WHAT I SEE
IN YOUR EYES WHEN YOU DO

140
00:05:11,812 --> 00:05:13,280
PHOTO SHOOTS--IT'S A SADNESS.

141
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,848
Sara: REALLY?
Tyra: MM-HMM.

142
00:05:14,848 --> 00:05:16,616
Sara: WOW.

143
00:05:16,616 --> 00:05:17,851
Shandi: NOW I'M STARTING TO
SEE MORE, LIKE, SERIOUSLY,

144
00:05:17,851 --> 00:05:19,486
I THINK I'VE GROWN MORE IN,
LIKE, THE PAST COUPLE OF WEEKS

145
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,555
THAN I HAVE GROWN, LIKE,
IN THE PAST COUPLE OF YEARS.

146
00:05:21,555 --> 00:05:24,291
AND IF I GO BACK HOME
TO, LIKE, MY LIFE...

147
00:05:24,291 --> 00:05:25,592
Tyra: I DON'T WANT YOU
TO GO BACK TO YOUR LIFE BEFORE,

148
00:05:25,592 --> 00:05:26,960
GOING,
"THERE'S ALWAYS WALGREENS."

149
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,328
Shandi: YEAH, EVERYONE'S
LIKE, "NO MORE WALGREENS

150
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,496
FOR SHANDI."

151
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:30,697
Tyra: LOOK AT THAT
AS YOUR PAST AND LOOK

152
00:05:30,697 --> 00:05:33,333
AT THIS WHOLE EXPERIENCE
AS BEING YOUR FUTURE.

153
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,668
Mercedes: OKAY.

154
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,503
Tyra: WELL, ONE THING
I WANNA TALK ABOUT WITH YOU

155
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:38,405
IS ON THE LAST PHOTO SHOOT,
I FELT LIKE YOU HAD

156
00:05:38,405 --> 00:05:39,806
AN ATTITUDE WITH PEOPLE.

157
00:05:39,806 --> 00:05:40,841
Mercedes: REALLY?

158
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:42,409
Tyra: YOU KNOW,
SO THAT'S JUST...

159
00:05:42,409 --> 00:05:44,644
Mercedes: THAT SHOOT,
THAT DAY, I WASN'T FEELING WELL.

160
00:05:44,644 --> 00:05:45,812
YOU THOUGHT I WAS GIVING
YOU ATTITUDE?

161
00:05:45,812 --> 00:05:47,581
Tyra: NOT ME,
JUST IN GENERAL.

162
00:05:47,581 --> 00:05:49,282
Mercedes: HAVING LUPUS--
I DON'T FEEL WELL,

163
00:05:49,282 --> 00:05:51,618
AND I'M TRYING TO HIDE IT,
AND I'M TRYING TO BE STRONG.

164
00:05:51,618 --> 00:05:52,786
Tyra: IF YOU GET ELIMINATED,
IT'S NOT GONNA BE BECAUSE

165
00:05:52,786 --> 00:05:55,355
YOU'RE TIRED AT WORK,
BUT IF I THINK THAT YOU HAVE

166
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:57,490
AN ATTITUDE AND YOU DON'T WORK
WELL WITH OTHERS, I'M GONNA BE

167
00:05:57,490 --> 00:05:58,758
LIKE, I DON'T KNOW ABOUT THAT.

168
00:05:58,758 --> 00:06:00,060
YOU KNOW?

169
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:01,761
SO JUST BE HONEST AND SPEAK UP.

170
00:06:01,761 --> 00:06:03,697
OKAY?

171
00:06:03,697 --> 00:06:05,966
Mercedes: I FEEL MYSELF
JUST DRAINING DOWN,

172
00:06:05,966 --> 00:06:08,735
BECAUSE I'M THINKING NEGATIVE,
I THINK I'M GONNA DIE.

173
00:06:08,735 --> 00:06:10,403
I THINK MY LIVER'S GONNA GO OUT.

174
00:06:10,403 --> 00:06:11,972
I'M HAVING SHORT TERM MEMORY.

175
00:06:11,972 --> 00:06:13,240
MY HAIR IS FALLING OUT.

176
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,342
I FEEL VULNERABLE. I FEEL WEAK.

177
00:06:15,342 --> 00:06:16,977
I'M HIDING ALL THESE THINGS.

178
00:06:16,977 --> 00:06:19,379
I'M JUST TIRED OF IT.

179
00:06:19,379 --> 00:06:22,349
SO WE WAKE UP, AND WE GO
TO, LIKE, LOWER EAST SIDE

180
00:06:22,349 --> 00:06:24,384
TO MEET THIS GENTLEMAN
BY THE NAME

181
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:27,821
OF STAN CHRISTENSEN
AND LEARN ABOUT OUR PERSONALITY.

182
00:06:27,821 --> 00:06:29,289
Stan: HI. I'M STAN.

183
00:06:29,289 --> 00:06:30,857
WE'RE WORKING TO GET THESE GIRLS
FAMILIAR WITH WHAT IT IS

184
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:34,394
ABOUT THEMSELVES THAT
OTHER PEOPLE IDENTIFY WITH,

185
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,363
SO THEY CAN TALK ABOUT
THEMSELVES COMFORTABLY WHEN

186
00:06:36,363 --> 00:06:38,798
THEY'RE IN INTERVIEW SITUATIONS.

187
00:06:38,798 --> 00:06:42,869
WHAT I'M GOING TO INTRODUCE
TO YOU IS THE MAGIC OF CHARISMA,

188
00:06:42,869 --> 00:06:45,372
HOW YOU CAN DRAW TO YOU
THE KIND OF ATTENTION

189
00:06:45,372 --> 00:06:47,741
THAT MAKES YOU STAND OUT,
THAT MAKES PEOPLE LISTEN,

190
00:06:47,741 --> 00:06:49,743
THAT MAKES PEOPLE NOTICE,
AND THAT'S PRETTY ESSENTIAL

191
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:51,645
TO A MODEL.

192
00:06:51,645 --> 00:06:52,946
Sara: YOU KNOW,
MODELING IS A PACKAGE DEAL.

193
00:06:52,946 --> 00:06:54,748
YOU HAVE TO LEARN HOW
TO WALK A RUNWAY

194
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:57,217
AND PORTRAY YOURSELF
IN A CERTAIN LIGHT.

195
00:06:57,217 --> 00:07:00,520
Stan: WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO IS
GATHER SOME INFORMATION

196
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:03,490
ABOUT HOW EVERYBODY ELSE
PERCEIVES US.

197
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:04,758
Sara: WE ARE HANDED
SHEETS OF PAPER,

198
00:07:04,758 --> 00:07:07,827
AND WE HAVE TO MARK OFF
ADJECTIVES THAT DESCRIBE

199
00:07:07,827 --> 00:07:09,829
EACH ONE OF THE GIRLS,
AND HE'S GONNA HAND THEM

200
00:07:09,829 --> 00:07:12,399
BACK TO THE GIRLS,
AND THEY GET TO SEE

201
00:07:12,399 --> 00:07:13,767
WHAT WE SAID ABOUT THEM.

202
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:15,335
Xiomara: IT'S A LOT.

203
00:07:15,335 --> 00:07:16,703
DO I HAVE TO SEE WHAT PEOPLE
THINK OF ME REALLY IN THE HOUSE?

204
00:07:16,703 --> 00:07:19,205
"ADVENTUROUS, HEADSTRONG."

205
00:07:19,205 --> 00:07:20,473
Yoanna: "STYLISH,
SOPHISTICATED."

206
00:07:20,473 --> 00:07:21,942
Shandi: "QUIRKY, FRAGILE."

207
00:07:21,942 --> 00:07:23,810
Catie: "SECRETIVE,
EMOTIONAL."

208
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:26,212
April: "RESPONSIBLE,
INTELLIGENT, SOPHISTICATED."

209
00:07:26,212 --> 00:07:27,647
Sara: "KIND, EXOTIC."

210
00:07:27,647 --> 00:07:30,951
Camille: "SUPERIOR,
RELENTLESS, HEADSTRONG, DEFIANT,

211
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:34,788
OUTSPOKEN, CUNNING, AGGRESSIVE,
OPINIONATED, DEMANDING

212
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:36,523
AND SINGLE-MINDED."

213
00:07:36,523 --> 00:07:38,425
Stan: ANYBODY SURPRISED?

214
00:07:38,425 --> 00:07:40,994
WHO FEELS ATTACKED?

215
00:07:40,994 --> 00:07:42,696
OKAY.

216
00:07:42,696 --> 00:07:44,597
Mercedes: CAMILLE WAS NOT
HAPPY WITH HER RESULTS.

217
00:07:44,597 --> 00:07:48,234
SHE WAS, LIKE, SUCKING
HER LIPS AND ROLLING HER EYES.

218
00:07:48,234 --> 00:07:50,570
Stan: CHARISMA IS ABOUT
THE WILLINGNESS TO DEAL

219
